> So far so good, except I am stuck on the part where you show loading whenever the query is running.

Could you detail a bit more "where you show loading whenever the query is running" => do you mean there's a documentation page where we show an interface displaying a "loading" mechanism and you do not understand how it works or smg else?

We do have a guide that explains how to read the search state: https://community.algolia.com/instantsearch.js/react/guides/conditional-display.html

And the state shape: https://community.algolia.com/instantsearch.js/react/guides/create-own-widget.html#getpropsprops-state-search-meta

But we have to make it better.

Here's an example:

```js
const Loading = createConnector({
    displayName: 'Loading',
    getProps(props, state, search) {
      return {loading: search.searching};
    },
 })(({loading}) => {
  console.log(loading);
 });
```
